  "notes": [
    "All configurations remain candidates for the exact OpenCode harness until they pass compatibility admission.",
    "Public evidence from another harness supports candidacy but does not qualify an OpenCode configuration.",
    "Configured does not mean currently available; the Runner must perform live provider preflight.",
    "2026-09-03: the nine OpenRouter configurations were removed from the registry. OpenRouter stays outside automatic routes by design (CODE_GENERATION_FLOW §4) and none of them could ever be selected; the provider remains available in opencode.json for manual use only.",
    "2026-09-08: certification by fixture was removed. Admission is membership in a route (decided from public benchmarks) plus, per project, a fit check the first time a configuration is used and the metalog of real calls. The order inside a role is computed from price, cheapest first, per provider tier; a configuration with two failures in a row attributable to the model sinks to the bottom until it succeeds again. Catalog statuses are active, watch, deprecated.",
    "2026-09-08: the Planner and the Goal Manager may use the authenticated OpenAI provider as their first tier (user's subscription); the OpenAI configurations are added with the benchmark rebuild.",
    "2026-09-08: Zen (provider opencode) left the registry by user decision: automatic routes use OpenCode Go and, for the Planner and the Goal Manager, the user's OpenAI subscription. The console's Use balance setting is outside this system; disabling it makes an exhausted Go quota stop the run as GO_USAGE_LIMIT.",
    "2026-09-08: admission is computed, never written by hand: lib/admission.mjs applies MODEL_SELECTION_SPEC §8 to config/benchmark-evidence.json (every score with its source; unconfirmed scores never count) and scripts/admit.mjs writes configurations and routes; tests/admission.test.mjs fails when the registry drifts from the rule. Preview, experimental, alpha, and contributor SKUs are registered as watch and never routed."
